meta {
  name: Create Regularization (too old - expect 400)
  type: http
  seq: 33
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/attendance/regularizations
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "work_date": "2024-01-15",
    "requested_status_name": "present",
    "reason": "Filed well outside the backdate window"
  }
}

docs {
  Negative case for the configurable backdate window.

  hr.attendance_rules.regularization_max_backdate_days (default 30) caps how far
  back a member may file. This work_date is years old, so it is outside any
  window an admin can set (the column is capped at 365).

  EXPECT 400 with a message naming the oldest acceptable date, e.g.
    "Regularizations are only accepted for the last 30 day(s) - on or after 2026-07-05."

  The window is counted in the ORG's timezone, not UTC, and the setting is
  edited in Attendance > Admin > Rules > Regularization (or via
  PUT /hr/attendance/rules/admin). Set it to 0 and even yesterday returns 400.
}
